# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# The build scripts and workflow files are consumed by Linux (GitHub Actions
# ubuntu-22.04, and the OpenWrt build itself). If any of them is checked out
# with CRLF, they break in ways that are hard to read:
#   * `diy-part2-25.12.sh`  -> "bash: ./diy-part2-25.12.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter"
#   * embedded heredocs      -> the terminator never matches ("EOF\r" != "EOF")
#   * .config / .append      -> stray CRs become part of values
#
# So pin LF explicitly for everything the build touches, regardless of the
# committer's platform or core.autocrlf setting.
#
# NOTE: *.dts/*.dtsi are deliberately NOT listed with text=auto, because the
# kernel device trees are plain LF and must stay byte-identical.

* text=auto

# This file itself, so it never gets rewritten on checkout either.
.gitattributes      text eol=lf

# Shell scripts -- must be LF, and must stay executable.
*.sh                text eol=lf
diy-part2*.sh       text eol=lf

# GitHub Actions workflows
*.yml               text eol=lf
*.yaml              text eol=lf

# Build inputs consumed on Linux
*.config            text eol=lf
.config*            text eol=lf
*.append            text eol=lf
*.lock              text eol=lf
*.diff              text eol=lf

# Device trees
*.dts               text eol=lf
*.dtsi              text eol=lf

# Documentation is rendered on Linux/CI and diffed across platforms; pin LF so
# a checkout on Windows cannot silently rewrite every line.
*.md                text eol=lf
*.txt               text eol=lf

# Binary-ish / generated artifacts: never touch
*.dtb               binary
*.bin               binary
*.ipk               binary
*.tar               binary
*.zst               binary
*.xz                binary
*.png               binary
*.jpg               binary
